{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Setting up the access role","context":"## Permissions policy\n\nAttach a policy that allows `bedrock:InvokeModel` on exactly the models\nthat your functions target.\n\n```\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Sid\": \"AllowInferenceFunctionModelInvocation\",\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": \"bedrock:InvokeModel\",\n \"Resource\": [\n \"[redacted ARN]\",\n \"[redacted ARN]\"\n ]\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\n**Note:**\n\nIf a function targets a cross-Region inference profile, grant both the\ninference-profile ARN and the foundation-model ARNs in each of the Regions that the\nprofile spans. This is an Amazon Bedrock requirement. For more information, see Set up an\ninference profile in the *Amazon Bedrock User\nGuide*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elemental-inference/latest/userguide/functions-prerequisites-access-role.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Getting started with cross-region inference in Amazon Bedrock | Artificial Intelligence","context":"### Identity and Access Management\n\nAWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) is key to securely managing your identities and access to AWS services and resources. Before you can use cross-region inference, check that your role has access to the cross-region inference API actions. For more details, see here.An example policy, which allows the caller to use the cross-region inference with the `InvokeModel*` APIs for any model in the `us-east-1` and `us-west-2` region is as follows:\n\n```\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n \"Action\": [\"bedrock:InvokeModel*\"],\n \"Resource: [\n \"arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1:<account_id>:inference-profile/*\",\n \"[redacted ARN]\",\n \"[redacted ARN]\"\n ]\n }\n ]\n}\n```","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/getting-started-with-cross-region-inference-in-amazon-bedrock/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"How do I resolve the \"AccessDeniedException\" error that I get when I use an Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference profile in an Organizations account?","context":"### Modify the IAM policy\n\n[Update your SCP](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_policies_update.html#update_policy) to include one of the following example policy statements.\n\n**Note:** In the following policy statements, replace **aa-example-1**, **aa-example-2**, **aa-example-3** with your Regions.\n\nDeny access to AWS services and resources from specified Regions except for Amazon Bedrock:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n \"NotAction\": \"bedrock:*\",\n \"Resource\": \"*\",\n \"Condition\": {\n \"StringEquals\": {\n \"aws:RequestedRegion\": [\n \"aa-example-1\",\n \"aa-example-2\",\n \"aa-example-3\"\n ]\n }\n }\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\nDeny actions to invoke a foundation model except through the inference profile in the specified Regions:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n \"Action\": [\n \"bedrock:InvokeModel\",\n \"bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream\"\n ],\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/*\",\n \"Condition\": {\n \"StringEquals\": {\n \"aws:RequestedRegion\": [\n \"aa-example-1\",\n \"aa-example-2\",\n \"aa-example-3\"\n ]\n },\n \"ArnNotLike\": {\n \"bedrock:InferenceProfileArn\": [\n \"arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:application-inference-profile/*\",\n \"arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/*\"\n ]\n }\n }\n }\n ]\n}\n```","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/bedrock-access-denied-exception"}]}}

