{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Prerequisites and permissions","context":"### Model invocation permissions\n\nWhen you create a job, Advanced Prompt Optimization invokes the target model(s) on\nyour behalf using your caller credentials (Forward Access Session). Your IAM\nidentity must have permission to invoke the specified models:\n\n| Inference Path | IAM Action Required | Resource ARN |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ConverseStream (current) | `bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` | `[redacted ARN]` |\n| Converse (non-streaming) | `bedrock:InvokeModel` | `[redacted ARN]` |\n| Cross-region inference profile | `bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` | `arn:aws:bedrock:*:account-id:inference-profile/profile-id` |\n| Application inference profile | `bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` | `arn:aws:bedrock:region:account-id:application-inference-profile/profile-id` |\n\n**Note:**\n\nYou can specify an application inference profile ARN as a target model in `modelConfigurations.modelId` and as a judge model in `customLLMJConfig.customLLMJModelId`. A judge model application inference profile must route to one of the supported judge models. The permission requirement is the same as invoking the application inference profile directly: your IAM identity needs permission to invoke the application inference profile plus the underlying inference profile and foundation model.\n\n**Important:**\n\nIf model access is not enabled for a model in your account, the job fails. The\nerror message is: \"No inference API is accessible for model. Verify that the\nrole has permission to invoke the model.\"","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/advanced-prompt-optimization-prereqs.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"How do I resolve the \"AccessDeniedException\" error that I get when I use an Amazon Bedrock cross-Region inference profile in an Organizations account?","context":"### Modify the IAM policy\n\n[Update your SCP](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_policies_update.html#update_policy) to include one of the following example policy statements.\n\n**Note:** In the following policy statements, replace **aa-example-1**, **aa-example-2**, **aa-example-3** with your Regions.\n\nDeny access to AWS services and resources from specified Regions except for Amazon Bedrock:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n \"NotAction\": \"bedrock:*\",\n \"Resource\": \"*\",\n \"Condition\": {\n \"StringEquals\": {\n \"aws:RequestedRegion\": [\n \"aa-example-1\",\n \"aa-example-2\",\n \"aa-example-3\"\n ]\n }\n }\n }\n ]\n}\n```\n\nDeny actions to invoke a foundation model except through the inference profile in the specified Regions:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n \"Statement\": [\n {\n \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n \"Action\": [\n \"bedrock:InvokeModel\",\n \"bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream\"\n ],\n \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/*\",\n \"Condition\": {\n \"StringEquals\": {\n \"aws:RequestedRegion\": [\n \"aa-example-1\",\n \"aa-example-2\",\n \"aa-example-3\"\n ]\n },\n \"ArnNotLike\": {\n \"bedrock:InferenceProfileArn\": [\n \"arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:application-inference-profile/*\",\n \"arn:aws:bedrock:*:*:inference-profile/*\"\n ]\n }\n }\n }\n ]\n}\n```","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/bedrock-access-denied-exception"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"How do I troubleshoot InvokeModel API errors in Amazon Bedrock?","context":"Resolution\n----------\n\n**AccessDeniedException** and **ValidationException** errors occur when the **InvokeModel** API can't access the base model that it's invoking. The errors can also occur if your AWS account doesn't have the required AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) permissions to run the operation","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/bedrock-invokemodel-api-error"}]}}

